accidentally,

528
00:30:21,282 --> 00:30:24,251
on purpose but didn't mean to,
but it just went down that way,

529
00:30:24,389 --> 00:30:26,114
catch Petey...

530
00:30:27,530 --> 00:30:28,772
You find the fish,
you find the cat.

531
00:30:30,360 --> 00:30:32,707
I mean, what's the mayor
gonna say? "That's not fair"?

532
00:30:32,845 --> 00:30:34,433
Life's not fair.

533
00:30:34,571 --> 00:30:36,539
Right?

534
00:30:36,677 --> 00:30:38,437
Hey, Dog Man, stop.
Dog Man, stop, stop, stop.

535
00:30:38,575 --> 00:30:39,680
Look, Dog Man, look.

536
00:30:39,818 --> 00:30:41,268
Are you ready?

537
00:30:41,406 --> 00:30:42,786
Good.

538
00:30:42,924 --> 00:30:44,857
Let's do this.

539
00:30:45,548 --> 00:30:47,135
Okay. Listen up.

540
00:30:47,274 --> 00:30:49,966
You're my clone, which means
evil runs through your veins.

541
00:30:50,104 --> 00:30:51,278
- Okay.
- You are destined

542
00:30:51,416 --> 00:30:52,624
- to be a villain.
- Ooh.

543
00:30:52,762 --> 00:30:54,453
- Is that fun?
- So much fun.

544
00:30:54,591 --> 00:30:56,006
- Yay!
- Of course,

545
00:30:56,144 --> 00:30:58,837
fun surrounded by, you know,
miserable suffering,

546
00:30:58,975 --> 00:31:01,219
loneliness and, like,
zero appreciation.

547
00:31:01,357 --> 00:31:03,013
I mean zero.

548
00:31:03,151 --> 00:31:04,083
Do you even know
what I'm saying?

549
00:31:04,222 --> 00:31:06,224
No, but it sounds fun.

550
00:31:06,362 --> 00:31:07,846
I want to be miserable, too.

551
00:31:07,984 --> 00:31:10,158
Good. That's the spirit.
Now, I got to go do something.

552
00:31:10,297 --> 00:31:11,367
- You stay put.
- Why?

553
00:31:11,505 --> 00:31:13,058
- Because you can't come.
- Why?

554
00:31:13,196 --> 00:31:15,094
Because it's serious business
and you're not ready yet.

555
00:31:15,233 --> 00:31:16,303
Why?

556
00:31:19,754 --> 00:31:22,343
I said you can't go.

557
00:31:22,481 --> 00:31:23,827
Why?

558
00:31:23,965 --> 00:31:25,243
Fine, but no talking.

559
00:31:25,381 --> 00:31:26,416
Do you have a car seat?

560
00:31:26,554 --> 00:31:28,176
- A what?
- A kid's car seat?

561
00:31:28,315 --> 00:31:30,213
You're a cloned cat sitting
in a flying mechanical bug.

562
00:31:30,351 --> 00:31:31,490
They don't make
a car seat for that.

563
00:31:31,628 --> 00:31:32,802
Okay, Papa.

564
00:31:32,940 --> 00:31:35,080
Stop calling me Papa.

565
00:31:35,218 --> 00:31:36,875
Okay.

566
00:31:37,634 --> 00:31:38,670
Papa.

567
00:31:38,808 --> 00:31:40,534
- I made you a book.
- What?

568
00:31:41,638 --> 00:31:44,296
Will you just hold on
and be quiet?

569
00:31:45,953 --> 00:31:48,127
- I need to go potty.
- Why?

570
00:31:48,266 --> 00:31:49,336
'Cause I need to.

571
00:31:49,474 --> 00:31:52,131
No, not "why." I know why.

572
00:31:52,270 --> 00:31:54,720
Sheesh. Just hold it.

573
00:31:57,965 --> 00:32:01,451
There it is,
the Living Spray Factory.

574
00:32:03,281 --> 00:32:05,559
Just a little closer.

575
00:32:08,596 --> 00:32:11,219
Ooh, what do these buttons do?

576
00:32:11,358 --> 00:32:13,912
- Pretty.
- Don't touch any...

577
00:32:15,362 --> 00:32:18,710
Woo-hoo!

578
00:32:25,406 --> 00:32:28,582
You almost got me killed...!

579
00:32:29,583 --> 00:32:30,998
Oh, no!

580
00:32:34,484 --> 00:32:35,830
Aah! It's stuck!

581
00:32:35,968 --> 00:32:37,694
Oh, great. Look what you did.

582
00:32:37,832 --> 00:32:39,938
It went down the wrong pipe,
and it's stuck.

583
00:32:40,076 --> 00:32:40,973
What is with you?

584
00:32:41,111 --> 00:32:42,941
I'm miserable.

585
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:45,461
Look, I don't need a kid.

586
00:32:45,599 --> 00:32:47,048
I didn't ask for a kid.
I don't want a kid!

587
00:32:47,186 --> 00:32:48,947
I got my own stuff to do,
and it's important.

588
00:32:49,085 --> 00:32:51,363
And when I say, "Don't touch
that button," you...

589
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:57,093
Shh.

590
00:32:57,990 --> 00:32:59,475
Shh, shh!

591
00:32:59,613 --> 00:33:01,580
No, hey. Shh.

592
00:33:02,754 --> 00:33:03,893
Shh!

593
00:33:04,031 --> 00:33:05,826
If you're gonna catch
that cat...

594
00:33:05,964 --> 00:33:08,035
you're gonna need
my special gear.

595
00:33:08,173 --> 00:33:10,071
Mm-hmm.

596
00:33:13,937 --> 00:33:16,595
All right, come on. Get in.

597
00:33:17,458 --> 00:33:18,908
Ugh.

598
00:33:19,598 --> 00:33:21,082
Come here.

599
00:33:42,552 --> 00:33:44,761
Oh, yeah.

600
00:33:47,350 --> 00:33:49,283
Okay, you put the little part--
this end, right?--

601
00:33:49,421 --> 00:33:51,630
up to your eyes, and then
the stuff that's far away

602
00:33:51,768 --> 00:33:54,288
will look really big, right?

603
00:33:54,426 --> 00:33:55,634
Yeah, you get it.

604
00:33:55,772 --> 00:33:56,911
All right, kid.

605
00:33:57,049 --> 00:33:58,223
- Get in.
- Why?

606
00:33:58,361 --> 00:33:59,914
Just get in.
We're gonna play a little game.

607
00:34:00,052 --> 00:34:01,709
Ooh. I hope it's "Miserable."

608
00:34:01,847 --> 00:34:03,331
It's called...

609
00:34:03,470 --> 00:34:05,575
the "New Home" game.

610
00:34:07,025 --> 00:34:09,268
This is just for pretend,
right?

611
00:34:09,407 --> 00:34:10,718
Of course.

612
00:34:11,650 --> 00:34:13,514
Ooh, a free kitty.

613
00:34:13,652 --> 00:34:15,033
How much does he cost?

614
00:34:15,171 --> 00:34:16,448
Uh, free.

615
00:34:16,586 --> 00:34:19,175
But I only have a dollar.

616
00:34:19,313 --> 00:34:20,728
A dollar?

617
00:34:21,591 --> 00:34:23,006
Can I get change?

618
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:25,181
Thank you.

619
00:34:25,319 --> 00:34:27,563
- What's your name?
- He doesn't have one.

620
00:34:27,701 --> 00:34:29,599
Yes, I do. I'm Li'l Petey.

621
00:34:29,737 --> 00:34:31,808
I think I'll call you Snowball.

622
00:34:31,946 --> 00:34:33,983
I think I'll call you
Poo-Poo Head.

623
00:34:34,121 --> 00:34:35,156
What?

624
00:34:35,294 --> 00:34:36,503
How rude!

625
00:34:36,641 --> 00:34:39,920
Here's your money back.

626
00:34:40,817 --> 00:34:41,991
I got to go potty.

627
00:34:42,129 --> 00:34:44,338
- Again?
- I didn't go last time.

628
00:34:44,476 --> 00:34:46,133
Wait, maybe I did.

629
00:34:46,271 --> 00:34:48,480
- No, I still got to go.
- What is wrong with people?

630
00:34:48,618 --> 00:34:50,275
"How much is the free kitty?"

631
00:34:50,413 --> 00:34:51,897
I don't know. Maybe it's free.

632
00:34:52,035 --> 00:34:56,488
I mean, it says it
right on the... box.

633
00:34:58,145 --> 00:35:00,112
Hey. Little cat?

634
00:35:00,250 --> 00:35:03,253
Uh, little dude?

635
00:35:03,391 --> 00:35:05,463
Hmm.

636
00:35:09,259 --> 00:35:10,606
Mm.

637
00:35:16,991 --> 00:35:18,545
Papa?

638
00:35:19,269 --> 00:35:21,064
Papa.

639
00:35:22,169 --> 00:35:23,998
Papa!

640
00:35:25,413 --> 00:35:27,036
Papa?

641
00:35:33,629 --> 00:35:35,562
Papa.

642
00:35:37,598 --> 00:35:39,497
Papa!

643
00:36:02,450 --> 00:36:03,555
Don't worry.

644
00:36:03,693 --> 00:36:05,799
- It'll be okay.
- Hmm?

645
00:36:18,052 --> 00:36:20,330
Good night, little crate.

646
00:36:21,193 --> 00:36:23,817
Don't be afraid.

647
00:37:30,573 --> 00:37:32,748
- Is that your house?
- Mm-hmm.

648
00:37:33,749 --> 00:37:36,372
Wow. It looks bigger
on the inside.

649
00:37:42,896 --> 00:37:45,726
- Is this where you sleep?
- Mm.

650
00:37:59,878 --> 00:38:01,846
Can you read me a story?

651
00:38:35,293 --> 00:38:38,261
Yep, solved that problem.

652
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:39,573
No more little kid.

653
00:38:39,711 --> 00:38:43,439
So now we can get back
to destroying Dog Man!

654
00:38:44,405 --> 00:38:45,752
Huh?

655
00:38:45,890 --> 00:38:48,962
"Papa and Me" by Li'l Petey.

656
00:38:50,653 --> 00:38:51,827
All right.

657
00:38:51,965 --> 00:38:56,003
"To Papa.
Papa and me are in the air.

658
00:38:56,141 --> 00:38:59,904
"It rained, and Papa and me
went into the lab.

659
00:39:00,042 --> 00:39:03,010
Look at Papa's new invention."

660
00:39:06,151 --> 00:39:10,190
"Papa and me think
the same thing."

661
00:39:13,572 --> 00:39:15,851
Ugh.

662
00:40:41,660 --> 00:40:44,387
Aw, Dog Man's got a friend.

663
00:40:48,598 --> 00:40:50,221
Huh?

664
00:41:33,195 --> 00:41:34,472
Dog Man, it's the chief.

665
00:41:34,610 --> 00:41:36,060
Who still has
an answering machine?

666
00:41:36,198 --> 00:41:38,303
Look, look. What is going on
with Petey, huh?

667
00:41:38,441 --> 00:41:40,167
Get back at me. It's important.

668
00:41:40,305 --> 00:41:43,550
Don't forget what's important.

669
00:41:55,320 --> 00:41:57,322
Janet?
Janet, what's that noise?

670
00:41:57,460 --> 00:41:59,014
Pressure's building
in the tanks.

671
00:41:59,152 --> 00:42:00,912
Something's clogging
the not-a-smokestack.

672
00:42:01,050 --> 00:42:02,189
What?

673
00:42:02,327 --> 00:42:04,191
Pressure supa high.

674
00:42:04,329 --> 00:42:06,021
Pressure supa high.

675
00:42:06,159 --> 00:42:08,816
Oh, no! Oh, no!

676
00:42:08,955 --> 00:42:10,680
Rocco!

677
00:42:10,818 --> 00:42:12,613
Gotcha.

678
00:42:12,751 --> 00:42:14,236
Ugh. "Cerealously"?

679
00:42:14,374 --> 00:42:15,582
Pressure supa high.

680
00:42:15,720 --> 00:42:17,895
What? Huh?

681
00:42:20,276 --> 00:42:22,037
Whew. That was it.

682
00:42:35,429 --> 00:42:37,052
At last!

683
00:42:37,915 --> 00:42:39,502
Huh.

684
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:44,059
Oh. Right.

685
00:42:53,758 --> 00:42:55,070
Yes!

686
00:42:55,208 --> 00:42:58,280
My 80 Hexotron Droid-Formigon
is complete.

687
00:42:58,418 --> 00:42:59,557
Hello.

688
00:43:01,283 --> 00:43:03,319
You're back.

689
00:43:03,457 --> 00:43:04,907
Finally came to your senses.

690
00:43:05,045 --> 00:43:07,013
No, I came to annoy you.

691
00:43:07,151 --> 00:43:08,186
Behold.

692
00:43:08,324 --> 00:43:10,326
What? I don't...

693
00:43:10,464 --> 00:43:12,328
So what?

694
00:43:12,466 --> 00:43:13,640
Dog Man?

695
00:43:13,778 --> 00:43:15,331
What? Dog Man?!

696
00:43:19,094 --> 00:43:20,819
Oh, yeah. You still owe me.

697
00:43:20,958 --> 00:43:21,959
I paid you.

698
00:43:22,097 --> 00:43:24,754
Bottle caps are not money!

699
00:43:24,892 --> 00:43:27,447
My clone with Dog Man?

700
00:43:28,931 --> 00:43:30,691
Oh, change of plans.

701
00:43:33,487 --> 00:43:36,732
I need you to scan this
and find the kid who made it.

702
00:43:40,770 --> 00:43:42,048
Well?

703
00:43:43,256 --> 00:43:44,429
Unbelievable.

704
00:43:44,567 --> 00:43:46,293
Well, don't just stand there.

705
00:43:46,431 --> 00:43:48,675
Go. Go, go, go, go get him.

706
00:44:03,655 --> 00:44:04,794
Oh, hi, Papa.

707
00:44:04,932 --> 00:44:06,900
What you doing?

708
00:44:07,038 --> 00:44:08,108
Getting you out of here
is what.

709
00:44:08,246 --> 00:44:09,213
How'd you find me?

710
00:44:09,351 --> 00:44:10,835
That's 80HD.

711
00:44:10,973 --> 00:44:13,182
He can find anybody. Come on.

712
00:44:14,287 --> 00:44:15,288
Hey, Papa.

713
00:44:15,426 --> 00:44:17,669
Look at this cute flowers.

714
00:44:17,807 --> 00:44:19,568
- Those are weeds.
- Oh.

715
00:44:19,706 --> 00:44:23,020
Hey, Papa.
Look at the pretty river.

716
00:44:23,158 --> 00:44:24,435
It's polluted.

717
00:44:24,573 --> 00:44:25,643
Oh.

718
00:44:26,437 --> 00:44:28,922
Hey, Papa.
Look at all the twinkly stars.

719
00:44:29,060 --> 00:44:31,166
Hey, you're standing in mud.

720
00:44:31,304 --> 00:44:32,857
Sheesh.

721
00:44:32,995 --> 00:44:34,997
That Dog Man's got you thinking
the whole world is just

722
00:44:35,135 --> 00:44:37,620
rainbows and unicorns
and lollipops.

723
00:44:37,758 --> 00:44:39,657
Ooh, lollipops. Hey.

724
00:44:39,795 --> 00:44:40,865
What about Dog Man?

725
00:44:41,003 --> 00:44:42,349
Oh, don't you worry.

726
00:44:42,487 --> 00:44:45,318
I got a special plan
to take care of Dog Man.

727
00:44:45,456 --> 00:44:48,562
The Squirrel Shooter 2000.

728
00:44:48,700 --> 00:44:50,771
Fun. Dog Man likes
to chase squirrels.

729
00:44:50,909 --> 00:44:53,567
Yeah, I'm kind of
counting on that.

730
00:45:00,816 --> 00:45:02,162
Time for bed.

731
00:45:12,034 --> 00:45:14,519
This is my room.

732
00:45:16,866 --> 00:45:19,559
And this is yours.

733
00:45:25,012 --> 00:45:26,876
I'm sleeping with you.

734
00:45:27,014 --> 00:45:28,257
- No, you're not.
- Yes, I am.

735
00:45:28,395 --> 00:45:29,500
No, you're not.

736
00:45:29,638 --> 00:45:30,880
- Yes, I am.
- No, you're not!

737
00:45:31,018 --> 00:45:32,330
Yes, I am.

738
00:45:32,468 --> 00:45:35,022
You're not sleeping with me,
and that's final.

739
00:45:38,405 --> 00:45:39,406
Yes, I am.

740
00:45:45,378 --> 00:45:46,689
Look, little guy...

741
00:45:48,277 --> 00:45:49,899
I want to give you the support
and guidance you need

742
00:45:50,037 --> 00:45:52,005
to be mean
and rotten-hearted like me.

743
00:45:52,143 --> 00:45:55,250
When I was a kid, my pop
didn't do anything for me.

744
00:45:55,388 --> 00:45:57,286
He got a truck,
he took all our stuff,

745
00:45:57,424 --> 00:45:59,150
and then he left
me and my mom all alone.

746
00:45:59,288 --> 00:46:01,083
- He did?
- Yep.

747
00:46:01,221 --> 00:46:02,843
I never saw him again.

748
00:46:09,609 --> 00:46:11,473
How come I made you

749
00:46:11,611 --> 00:46:12,991
but you're not like me?

750
00:46:13,130 --> 00:46:16,202
Maybe I am, but you just
don't like that part.

751
00:46:18,411 --> 00:46:20,792
Oh, I know.
Let's go find your papa.

752
00:46:20,930 --> 00:46:23,726
Maybe he's changed.
Maybe he's sorry.

753
00:46:23,864 --> 00:46:25,590
Look, I know you think
everybody is a good guy

754
00:46:25,728 --> 00:46:28,145
deep down inside,
but that's just not reality.

755
00:46:28,283 --> 00:46:29,870
The world's a horrible place.

756
00:46:30,008 --> 00:46:32,632
It's mostly misery
and selfishness out there.

757
00:46:32,770 --> 00:46:34,323
That's reality.

758
00:46:35,462 --> 00:46:36,670
I'm sleeping with you.

759
00:46:36,808 --> 00:46:37,982
No, you're...

760
00:47:35,246 --> 00:47:38,732
When you find my grampa,
bring him back here, okay?

761
00:48:01,859 --> 00:48:04,413
Hey, Dog Man.

762
00:48:05,242 --> 00:48:06,864
- How's it going?
- Ruff!

763
00:48:07,002 --> 00:48:08,175
I'll be right over.

764
00:48:09,453 --> 00:48:11,593
Dog Man, what happened?

765
00:48:17,875 --> 00:48:19,463
Sarah!

766
00:48:19,601 --> 00:48:21,016
Yes. Sarah Hatoff here,

767
00:48:21,154 --> 00:48:23,363
reporting live
from Dog Man's house.

768
00:48:23,501 --> 00:48:25,262
Have you seen this cat?

769
00:48:25,400 --> 00:48:27,402
He disappeared overnight.

770
00:48:27,540 --> 00:48:29,473
Dog Man, wait! Wait up!

771
00:48:33,649 --> 00:48:36,376
Where, oh, where
has this little cat gone?

772
00:48:36,514 --> 00:48:37,791
Where would you find
a little kitty?

773
00:48:37,929 --> 00:48:39,793
Oh, of course.

774
00:48:40,863 --> 00:48:42,693
Yarn Yurt.

775
00:48:49,424 --> 00:48:51,495
Mice & Cheese-y? Good idea.

776
00:48:53,290 --> 00:48:54,739
Nothing?

777
00:48:56,051 --> 00:48:57,604
What about
The Indifferent Shop?

778
00:48:57,742 --> 00:49:00,055
"Go away or not.
I don't care." Hmm.

779
00:49:00,193 --> 00:49:01,677
Chuckie's Things You Chuck?

780
00:49:01,815 --> 00:49:03,300
Laser Pointer Palace?

781
00:49:03,438 --> 00:49:04,749
Cozy Cat Carpet Club?

782
00:49:04,887 --> 00:49:06,820
Kibble McNibble?
Hot Tin Woof? Ears for Fears?

783
00:49:11,031 --> 00:49:12,032
Uh...

784
00:49:14,725 --> 00:49:16,243
We've checked all over town.

785
00:49:16,382 --> 00:49:17,659
We found nothing.

786
00:49:17,797 --> 00:49:19,039
Well, except in the sandbox.

787
00:49:19,177 --> 00:49:20,247
Ew.

788
00:49:20,386 --> 00:49:22,249
So, if you see this cat,

789
00:49:22,388 --> 00:49:24,251
please return him to Dog Man.

790
00:49:24,390 --> 00:49:25,529
My clone?

791
00:49:25,667 --> 00:49:28,325
Return him to Dog Man? Ha!

792
00:49:28,463 --> 00:49:30,430
Well, you can't return him
to Dog Man

793
00:49:30,568 --> 00:49:32,777
if there is no Dog Man.

794
00:49:34,089 --> 00:49:35,159
Doorbell.

795
00:49:35,297 --> 00:49:36,540
Hmm?

796
00:49:39,232 --> 00:49:40,475
Wha... Hey!

